    <LoopInitiator loopType="TrialHandler" name="first_loop">
      <Param name="Selected rows" updates="None" val="$conditionSelector" valType="str"/>
      <Param name="conditions" updates="None" val="[{'question': 'Why is an interdisciplinary approach important in the Human and AI master programme that brings together psychology, philosophy, and computer science?', 'answer': 'From a computer science perspective, an interdisciplinary Human and AI programme is crucial because technical systems never exist in a vacuum. We can design elegant algorithms, but once they are deployed, they interact with human attention, bias, and social norms. Working with psychologists helps us understand how people actually interpret model outputs, when they over-trust or under-trust them, and how interfaces can support better decisions. Philosophy contributes by clarifying normative questions: what does it mean for an AI system to be fair, transparent, or accountable, and which values should be encoded in design choices. Without these perspectives, computer scientists risk optimising for metrics that are technically impressive but socially harmful. Interdisciplinarity forces us to think not just about what AI can do, but what it should do and for whom.', 'perspective': 'CS', 'source_type': 'AI'}, {'question': 'Why is an interdisciplinary approach important in the Human and AI master programme that brings together psychology, philosophy, and computer science?', 'answer': 'From a psychology perspective, the value of an interdisciplinary Human and AI programme lies in treating AI systems as part of people’s cognitive environment. Human beings do not simply use tools; they adapt their attention, memory, and decision strategies to the tools available. AI-based systems shape how people distribute trust, how they experience control or helplessness, and how they form beliefs about evidence and expertise. Studying these processes requires collaboration with computer scientists, who can explain how models are built and what kinds of errors they tend to make, and with philosophers, who can frame questions about agency, responsibility, and explanation. Interdisciplinarity allows psychologists to design studies and interventions that are not just about technology use in general, but about concrete AI architectures and their psychological consequences.', 'perspective': 'Psychology', 'source_type': 'AI'}, {'question': 'Why is an interdisciplinary approach important in the Human and AI master programme that brings together psychology, philosophy, and computer science?', 'answer': 'From a philosophical perspective, an interdisciplinary Human and AI programme is vital because it forces us to confront questions that cannot be answered from within a single discipline. AI systems challenge our concepts of agency, explanation, knowledge, and responsibility. Philosophers can help articulate what it means to understand a model’s output, to give a justification rather than just a prediction, or to assign moral responsibility when decisions are distributed across humans and machines. However, these questions must be informed by psychological evidence about how people actually reason with AI systems, and by technical understanding of what current models can and cannot represent. Interdisciplinarity prevents purely abstract speculation and purely technical optimisation, connecting normative reflection with empirical constraints.', 'perspective': 'Philosophy', 'source_type': 'AI'}, {'question': 'Why is an interdisciplinary approach important in the Human and AI master programme that brings together psychology, philosophy, and computer science?', 'answer': 'This is the human version from the computer science perspective. (Will be replaced with a real human-written answer later.)', 'perspective': 'CS', 'source_type': 'human'}, {'question': 'Why is an interdisciplinary approach important in the Human and AI master programme that brings together psychology, philosophy, and computer science?', 'answer': 'This is the human version from the psychology perspective. (Will be replaced with a real human-written answer later.)', 'perspective': 'Psychology', 'source_type': 'human'}, {'question': 'Why is an interdisciplinary approach important in the Human and AI master programme that brings together psychology, philosophy, and computer science?', 'answer': 'This is the human version from the philosophy perspective. (Will be replaced with a real human-written answer later.)', 'perspective': 'Philosophy', 'source_type': 'human'}]" valType="str"/>
      <Param name="conditionsFile" updates="None" val="first_content.xlsx" valType="file"/>
      <Param name="endPoints" updates="None" val="[0, 1]" valType="num"/>
      <Param name="isTrials" updates="None" val="True" valType="bool"/>
      <Param name="loopType" updates="None" val="random" valType="str"/>
      <Param name="nReps" updates="None" val="1" valType="num"/>
      <Param name="name" updates="None" val="first_loop" valType="code"/>
      <Param name="random seed" updates="None" val="" valType="code"/>
    </LoopInitiator>
